{
  "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixtures for the Claude Code table ('reproduced in conformance/fixtures/mappings/ as they gain fixtures'). First entry (AEP-0006): AskUserQuestion -> one attention.requested(kind:'form') per tool call — one event for the whole 1-4 question batch, one field_spec per question. run.js pins impl/adapter-claude-code/map-ask-user-question.js (the adapter's own mapping) against expected_data; run.py — spec-only, no adapter implementation — checks each expected payload against the attention.requested schema and the wire facts the mapping must guarantee (kind form, one field per question, other:true on every field, multi mirrors multiSelect).",
  "ask_user_question": {
    "$comment": "expected_data is the emitted `data` payload at capture redacted+ (real labels through the §9.4 pipeline); expected_data_metadata is the same call at capture metadata — labels degrade to structural placeholders per the field_spec.label/choices[].label [metadata*] exception. Field/choice ids are 1-based indexes so answer.values stays structural at any ceiling. The adapter assembles data as {kind:'form', ...mapping, respond_via:['control']}.",
    "input": {
      "questions": [
        {
          "question": "Which database should the new service use?",
          "header": "Database",
          "multiSelect": false,
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "PostgreSQL",
              "description": "relational, ACID"
            },
            {
              "label": "SQLite",
              "description": "embedded, zero-ops"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "Which regions should we roll out to?",
          "header": "Regions",
          "multiSelect": true,
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "us-east"
            },
            {
              "label": "eu-west"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "expected_data": {
      "kind": "form",
      "prompt": "claude-code asks 2 questions",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "Database: Which database should the new service use?",
          "required": true,
          "other": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "PostgreSQL"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "SQLite"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "Regions: Which regions should we roll out to?",
          "required": true,
          "other": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "us-east"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "eu-west"
            }
          ],
          "multi": true
        }
      ],
      "respond_via": [
        "control"
      ]
    },
    "expected_data_metadata": {
      "kind": "form",
      "prompt": "claude-code asks 2 questions",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "1",
          "required": true,
          "other": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "2",
          "required": true,
          "other": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2"
            }
          ],
          "multi": true
        }
      ],
      "respond_via": [
        "control"
      ]
    }
  },
  "elicitation": {
    "$comment": "Second Annex A pin (MCP elicitation -> AEP-0006 form): Claude Code's Elicitation hook surfaces an MCP server's elicitation/create request (message + restricted flat schema). Field ids are the schema property KEYS and enum choice ids the enum VALUES (both structural, server-defined), so accepted answer.values map back to the elicitation content verbatim; title/enumNames are display content — present at redacted+ (expected_data), degraded to the structural key/value at metadata (expected_data_metadata). MCP elicitation enums are CLOSED: no other:true escape, unlike AskUserQuestion. run.js pins impl/adapter-claude-code/map-elicitation.js against these; run.py checks schema validity + the wire facts.",
    "input": {
      "message": "Configure the deployment target",
      "requestedSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "environment": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "staging",
              "production"
            ],
            "enumNames": [
              "Staging",
              "Production"
            ],
            "title": "Environment"
          },
          "replicas": {
            "type": "integer",
            "title": "Replica count"
          },
          "reason": {
            "type": "string",
            "title": "Why now"
          },
          "confirm": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "title": "Proceed immediately"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "environment",
          "confirm"
        ]
      }
    },
    "expected_data": {
      "kind": "form",
      "prompt": "Configure the deployment target",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "environment",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "Environment",
          "required": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "staging",
              "label": "Staging"
            },
            {
              "id": "production",
              "label": "Production"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "replicas",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "Replica count",
          "required": false
        },
        {
          "id": "reason",
          "type": "string",
          "label": "Why now",
          "required": false
        },
        {
          "id": "confirm",
          "type": "boolean",
          "label": "Proceed immediately",
          "required": true
        }
      ],
      "respond_via": [
        "control"
      ]
    },
    "expected_data_metadata": {
      "kind": "form",
      "prompt": "claude-code requests input (4 fields)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "environment",
          "type": "select",
          "label": "environment",
          "required": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "staging",
              "label": "staging"
            },
            {
              "id": "production",
              "label": "production"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "replicas",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "replicas",
          "required": false
        },
        {
          "id": "reason",
          "type": "string",
          "label": "reason",
          "required": false
        },
        {
          "id": "confirm",
          "type": "boolean",
          "label": "confirm",
          "required": true
        }
      ],
      "respond_via": [
        "control"
      ]
    }
  }
}
